        "tekst": "**If you only remember 8 things**\n\n1. The executive is the top slice; governing without it is impossible; executives are politically accountable, bureaucracies are not.\n2. Head of state (dignified) against head of government (efficient): Bagehot.\n3. Four executives: presidential, parliamentary, semi-presidential, authoritarian; constitutional limits make the difference.\n4. Majority, coalition and minority government; prime ministerial, cabinet and ministerial models.\n5. Semi-presidential subtypes and cohabitation; authoritarian personalism.\n6. Bureaucracy: rule by officials; advice and implementation; Weber's five features against the lecture's five principles.\n7. Spoils system and Pendleton Act, outsourcing, new public management, e-government.\n8. Departments, divisions, NDPBs; unified against departmental recruitment; whistleblowing and the ombudsman; developmental against predatory states."
