        "type": "slimmer",
        "tekst": "**Part 2 in one breath**\n\nParties govern, guide, aggregate, mobilise and recruit, but voters are less attached than before. Parties range from cadre and mass to catch-all, niche and cartel, in five kinds of party system. Elites tend to run parties (Michels), whoever selects the candidates owns the party, and in authoritarian states the party is the vehicle, not the driver."
